# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and built into linux/amd64 images. A shell
# script checked out with CRLF is copied into the image verbatim, and the
# kernel then reads the shebang as "/bin/sh\r", which does not exist. The
# failure surfaces as `not found` naming a file that is plainly present, so
# pin every executable text format to LF regardless of host.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
